.TH AGY 1 "June 2026" "agy-cli v0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agy \- Antigravity CLI workflow engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agy
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agy
is the core command-line workflow engine for Antigravity (Gemini CLI), optimized for stats researchers working on causal inference and managing Obsidian/Atlas subprojects. It provides concurrent assumption validation (Positivity, Exchangeability, SUTVA, and Covariate Balance), git worktree management with virtualenv dependency caching, and bidirectional Atlas session tracking.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show helper messages and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Core Validation
.TP
.B eval \fR[\fISTUDY_DESIGN_FILE\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Concurrently evaluate observational study assumptions (Positivity, Exchangeability, SUTVA, and Covariate Balance).
.RS
.TP
.BI \-t\fR,\fB \-\-treatment\fR \fINAME\fR
Specify the treatment (exposure) variable name.
.TP
.BI \-o\fR,\fB \-\-outcome\fR \fINAME\fR
Specify the outcome variable name.
.TP
.BI \-c\fR,\fB \-\-covariates\fR \fILIST\fR
Comma-separated list of covariate names.
.TP
.BI \-d\fR,\fB \-\-data\fR \fIPATH\fR
Path to observational data CSV file.
.TP
.BI \-g\fR,\fB \-\-dag\-str\fR \fISTRING\fR
Causal graph description in DAG format (e.g., 'W -> Y, X -> W, X -> Y').
.TP
.B \-\-interactive / \-\-non\-interactive
Enable or disable interactive SUTVA survey prompts.
.TP
.BI \-\-method\fR \fIMETHOD\fR
Specify propensity score adjustment method: none, matching, or weighting (default: none).
.RE
.TP
.B dag \fISTRING\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Compile textual causal graph description to R ggdag/dagitty code.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-o\fR,\fB \-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR
Output compiled R code directly to the specified file path.
.TP
.BI \-t\fR,\fB \-\-treatment\fR \fINAME\fR
Inject exposure metadata.
.TP
.BI \-y\fR,\fB \-\-outcome\fR \fINAME\fR
Inject outcome metadata.
.RE
.SS Worktree & Caching
.TP
.B worktree add \fINAME\fR
Create a persistent feature worktree off the dev branch, tracking it inside .STATUS and symlinking the root .venv for sub-10ms dependency caching.
.TP
.B worktree list
List currently active/registered git worktrees.
.TP
.B worktree remove \fINAME\fR
Decommission the worktree and delete its local feature branch.
.SS R Package Bridge
.TP
.B rforge check
Run package check via devtools::check(document = FALSE).
.TP
.B rforge test
Run package unit tests via devtools::test().
.TP
.B rforge document
Compile Roxygen2 documentation via devtools::document().
.SS Plugins & Bridges
.TP
.B obs orphans
List notes with no connections ($k_{in} = 0$, $k_{out} = 0$).
.TP
.B obs hubs \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
List central notes. Options: --limit <INT> (default 10), --sort <pagerank|out_degree|in_degree|total_degree>.
.TP
.B obs health
Verify graph connections for broken note links.
.TP
.B atlas status
Show active project session status and elapsed duration.
.TP
.B atlas trail \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Display recent workspace breadcrumbs. Options: --limit <INT> (default 10).
.TP
.B atlas start\-session \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Start a new active Atlas session. Options: --project <NAME> (required), --task <TASK> (required), --desc <TEXT>.
.TP
.B atlas log\-crumb \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fITEXT\fR
Log a custom breadcrumb to the registry. Options: --type <TYPE> (default "command"), --project <NAME>.
.TP
.B sandbox generate \fIPATH\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Generate a temporary mock vault containing notes, databases, and causal CSV data. Options: --violations (inject positivity, exchangeability, and SUTVA violations).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AGY_LOG_FILE
Path to the central error log file. Default: ~/.config/obs/obs.log
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/obs/obs.log
Central rotating log file (5MB limit, 3 backups) capturing timestamps, log levels, and stack traces for unhandled CLI errors.
.TP
.I .STATUS
Project status tracker and worktree registry.
.TP
.I ~/.git\-worktrees/agy\-cli
Default parent directory for isolated git worktrees.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run concurrent validation on study assumptions:
.RS
.nf
agy eval -t W -o Y -c X -d ./data.csv -g "X -> W, X -> Y, W -> Y" --non-interactive
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compile DAG to R script:
.RS
.nf
agy dag "W -> Y, X -> W, X -> Y" -t W -y Y -o my_dag.R
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start active session tracking in Atlas:
.RS
.nf
agy atlas start-session --project agy-cli --task "man alignment" --desc "Rewriting agy.1 man page"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add a new feature worktree:
.RS
.nf
agy worktree add feature-docs
.fi
.RE
